---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ArticleCTA from '../../components/ArticleCTA.astro';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  '@id': 'https://www.savemygig.com/fix/waveforms-not-loading-cdj#article',
  headline: 'Waveforms Not Loading on CDJ - What It Means',
  description: 'Tracks play but waveforms stay blank or take forever on the CDJ. Missing analysis, slow drives, or a struggling database, here\'s the fix order.',
  author: { '@id': 'https://www.savemygig.com/#org' },
  publisher: { '@id': 'https://www.savemygig.com/#org' },
  datePublished: '2026-07-24',
  dateModified: '2026-07-27',
  inLanguage: 'en',
  // ARTICLE IMAGE (2026-08-04). Google's Article guidance asks for an image,
  // and without one an Article node is never a candidate for a rich result.
  // This is the article's own share card, generated from its own title by
  // scripts/gen-og.mjs, so it represents this article and nothing else.
  // mainEntityOfPage is an @id reference rather than a bare URL string so it
  // resolves to the WebPage node Base.astro emits, instead of being a URL
  // that merely looks like one.
  mainEntityOfPage: { '@id': 'https://www.savemygig.com/fix/waveforms-not-loading-cdj#webpage' },
  image: 'https://www.savemygig.com/og/waveforms-not-loading-cdj.png',
};
---
<Base
  title="Waveforms Not Loading on CDJ? Causes and Fixes | Save My Gig"
  description="Tracks play but waveforms stay blank or take forever on the CDJ. Missing analysis, slow drives, or a struggling database, here's the fix order."
  path="/fix/waveforms-not-loading-cdj"
  crumbName="Waveforms not loading"
  ogImage="/og/waveforms-not-loading-cdj.png"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" slot="head" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
  <main class="wrap wrap-wide">
    <div class="status-line red">Waveforms_Blank</div>
    <h1 style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">WAVEFORMS <span class="danger">NOT LOADING</span>?<br>Read this first</h1>

    <div class="panel panel-go">
      <p style="margin:0"><strong>Short version:</strong> blank waveforms almost never stop a set. The audio plays fine, you are missing convenience, not music. Fix order below.</p>
    </div>

        {/* FIRST SECTION OPEN ON ARRIVAL (H5, 2026-08-05). The h1 above says
            "DO THIS, IN THIS ORDER" and this page used to answer it with three
            closed rows: zero instructions on screen for someone who is already
            panicking. The first row is the fastest checks, which is what
            everyone needs first, so it is server-rendered open. The rest stay
            closed, and the exclusive `name` still means opening another closes
            this one. `open` on the element, never JavaScript: it has to be in
            the initial HTML and it has to survive JS being off. */}
        <details class="acc-sec" name="fix-acc" open>
      <summary><h2 class="acc-h2">The three causes</h2><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li><strong>Tracks were never analyzed.</strong> Files dragged manually (or imported and exported too fast) carry no waveform data. The player shows a slowly-building wave or nothing.</li>
      <li><strong>The drive is slow or dying.</strong> Waveform data loads from the USB; a struggling drive shows tracks instantly but waveforms crawl. Treat this as an early warning.</li>
      <li><strong>Database mismatch.</strong> Old player firmware + new rekordbox versions occasionally skip detailed waveform data. Audio still plays.</li>
    </ul>

    
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="acc-sec" name="fix-acc">
      <summary><h2 class="acc-h2">At the venue</h2><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>Play on. The wave draws in real time as the player reads the track, beatmatch by ear like the veterans did.</li>
      <li>If waveforms crawl AND browsing lags: the drive is struggling. Don't trust it for the next gig - <a href="/fix/usb-not-recognized-cdj">this is how those drives end</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="acc-sec" name="fix-acc">
      <summary><h2 class="acc-h2">At home</h2><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>In rekordbox: select your library → right-click → <strong>Analyze</strong>. Let it finish completely.</li>
      <li>Re-export tonight's playlists in <span class="mono" translate="no">EXPORT</span> mode; the analysis travels with the export.</li>
      <li>Update player firmware and rekordbox to the versions your gear supports.</li>
      <li>Full-format (not quick) the suspect drive; if it crawls, retire it. <a href="/gear">Drives that don't do this →</a></li>
    </ul>
      </div>
    </details>



    <ArticleCTA article="waveforms" />
  </main>
</Base>
